A||||2||rodmcneill||Washer no squirty.||||1||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||12-28-2001||01:30 PM||||I replaced my windshield water pump,I have replaced the circuit board with a known good one, still no pump action. There is a ground G201 that I am going to check, does anyone know EXACTLY where this is under the dash. On the old circuit board I cleaned up all the connections got 2 squirts then nothing. This is driving me nuts! If I cannot find the problem I will just run a straight wire to the pump with a toggle switch but I would rather try to fix it. Any input would be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||BC-GT||12-28-2001||07:56 PM||||Well I just did everything that you described but got about 6 "squirts" out of it, tried 4 different boards and 2 different washer pumps. Turned out to be my Wiper motor was bad, I think it was shorting out inside somewhere(the washer pump circuit also goes through the wiper motor). When I shorted the washer pump at the wiper motor, it would work occasionaly, then it started to just blow fuses. Anyway, try swapping a wiper motor in, it worked for me. For more details visit this page and click on the "delay wiper operation" link. <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rodmcneill||12-28-2001||11:50 PM||||Thanks for the info.||||reg||14
